  "name": "Track TikTok videos for any keyword in Google Sheets with viral alerts in Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "59143138-78df-4f3e-aebc-169ce946cf17",
      "name": "Sticky Note -1060_-560",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1060,
        -560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1480,
        "content": "## TikTok keyword tracker with breakout alerts\n\n## Who's it for\n\nSocial media managers, trend researchers, and e-commerce brands tracking what's taking off on TikTok in their niche.\n\n## How it works\n\nEvery morning the workflow searches TikTok via API Direct (pay-as-you-go, from $0.002/request) for your keyword's most recent videos, skips everything it already logged on earlier runs, and appends each new video to a Google Sheet — author, title, plays, likes, shares, comments, and link. Over days the sheet becomes a trend dataset you can sort, chart, and mine for creators to work with. And when a video crosses your play-count threshold, it's pushed to Slack immediately — so you catch breakouts while they're breaking, not in next week's report.\n\nThis template uses the [API Direct](https://apidirect.io) verified community node — available on n8n Cloud and self-hosted n8n (search “API Direct” in the nodes panel). No official API access, developer accounts, or OAuth apps needed.\n\n## How to set up\n\n1. Create an [API Direct](https://apidirect.io) account, copy your API key, and add it as a credential in the TikTok node (new accounts include free credit).\n2. Open **Edit your keyword settings** — set your niche keyword and the viral threshold (plays).\n3. Create a Google Sheet with the header row: `date, author, title, url, plays, likes, shares, comments`, and pick it in the Google Sheets node.\n4. Connect Slack and pick the channel for breakout alerts.\n5. Activate the workflow (the seen-video memory only persists on active workflows).\n\n## Requirements\n\n- API Direct API key\n- Google account for Sheets\n- Slack workspace (for breakout alerts)\n\n## How to customize\n\n- Switch the search to Instagram, YouTube, or Twitter/X by changing the resource on the search node.\n- Tune the viral threshold per niche — 100k plays is huge for B2B, small for dance.\n- Track engagement rate instead: alert when likes/plays is unusually high.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "33b0eee3-1217-49e3-aa9a-5b0956a45aeb",
      "name": "Sticky Note -420_-340",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -420,
        -340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "### How it flows\nSearch TikTok (last 24h, most recent first) → drop already-logged videos → log every new video to Google Sheets → videos above your play threshold also ping Slack.\n\nSheet header row:\n`date, author, title, url, plays, likes, shares, comments`\n\nAlready-seen results are remembered between runs (n8n workflow static data), so daily runs only process new items. The memory starts working once the workflow is **activated** — manual test runs always process everything."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a007fdde-e22b-42c7-9444-99c06434d20c",
      "name": "Every morning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        -340,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "days",
              "triggerAtHour": 8
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
